WEBVTT

00:00:08.990 --> 00:00:11.690
My brother... is here...

00:00:11.690 --> 00:00:15.190
He's right out there!

00:00:15.190 --> 00:00:19.570
But I can't even go into space...

00:00:19.570 --> 00:00:23.370
Why am I here?! Why?!

00:00:34.210 --> 00:00:36.110
Let's go, Emily...

00:00:55.530 --> 00:00:58.140
I'm coming, Brother!

00:00:59.030 --> 00:01:03.540
Reasoner Sara

00:01:04.160 --> 00:01:07.030
Ralph Werec! He's here!

00:01:07.030 --> 00:01:09.570
I won't let this chance get away!

00:01:09.570 --> 00:01:11.500
He dodged it?!

00:01:11.500 --> 00:01:12.490
Oh no!

00:01:31.490 --> 00:01:34.460
What is that?! It looks
like a Strain, but...

00:01:34.460 --> 00:01:36.160
You okay, Lottie?!

00:01:36.160 --> 00:01:37.230
Carrisford!

00:01:37.230 --> 00:01:38.730
Did you see that Strain?!

00:01:38.730 --> 00:01:40.600
Who's its Reasoner?!

00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:42.500
Brother!

00:01:42.500 --> 00:01:44.870
I know you can hear me! Answer!

00:01:44.870 --> 00:01:47.570
Answer me, Brother!

00:01:47.570 --> 00:01:49.060
Why?!

00:01:54.810 --> 00:01:58.350
Dunno who it is,
but I'm killing that man!

00:01:58.350 --> 00:02:00.220
I won't let anyone else have him!

00:02:03.990 --> 00:02:05.160
What are you doing?!

00:02:05.160 --> 00:02:07.330
Move! Stay out of my way!

00:02:07.330 --> 00:02:08.760
You?!

00:02:08.760 --> 00:02:09.920
Wait!

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:18.270
Operator! Do you have a fix on the Gloire?

00:02:18.270 --> 00:02:21.840
Y-yes, sir! It appears to be locked
in combat with a Strain-like unit

00:02:21.840 --> 00:02:23.840
that launched from our ship moments ago!

00:02:23.840 --> 00:02:27.450
What do you mean, "like"?!
Give accurate reports!

00:02:27.450 --> 00:02:28.610
S-sorry, sir!

00:02:28.610 --> 00:02:32.920
It's definitely a Strain, but I'm
not detecting our ID code from it...

00:02:32.920 --> 00:02:36.190
A unit of unknown origin?
Where did it come from?

00:02:36.190 --> 00:02:39.360
Them, obviously.

00:02:39.360 --> 00:02:44.130
It works! My Strain works! Hurray!

00:02:44.130 --> 00:02:50.470
It's as mobile as a Gloire
and has a powerful form!

00:02:50.470 --> 00:02:53.030
I'm such a genius!

00:02:54.540 --> 00:02:57.170
He's way too carefree, that's for sure...

00:02:59.710 --> 00:03:00.870
Brother!

00:03:19.400 --> 00:03:22.130
What an incredible display of dexterity!

00:03:22.130 --> 00:03:25.660
To think it can fight on
even terms with a Gloire...

00:03:27.340 --> 00:03:28.640
Situation!

00:03:28.640 --> 00:03:30.980
TUMOR concentration on the port quarter!

00:03:30.980 --> 00:03:32.940
They're attempting to attach to the ship!

00:03:32.940 --> 00:03:35.910
Don't tell me they're trying to get inside?!

00:03:35.910 --> 00:03:38.120
Where is the Strain squadron?!

00:03:38.120 --> 00:03:39.580
The TUMORs are behaving cleverly enough

00:03:39.580 --> 00:03:41.580
that they can't get near the Libertad!

00:03:54.800 --> 00:03:57.270
How odd. There's something
strange about this...

00:03:57.270 --> 00:03:58.370
Strange?

00:03:58.370 --> 00:03:59.200
Yes, sir.

00:03:59.200 --> 00:04:02.310
The enemy has enough firepower
to take down two escort ships

00:04:02.310 --> 00:04:04.010
in the blink of an eye.

00:04:04.010 --> 00:04:07.610
But now they're going through
the trouble of getting inside ours.

00:04:07.610 --> 00:04:11.680
It's possible that this ship's
destruction isn't their goal.

00:04:11.680 --> 00:04:14.320
You're saying there could
be some other goal?

00:04:14.320 --> 00:04:16.560
All Gambees in Trenches 3 through 8,

00:04:16.560 --> 00:04:19.060
pull off all TUMORs attached to the ship!

00:04:19.060 --> 00:04:21.390
Do not let the enemy inside!

00:04:26.770 --> 00:04:28.930
Yes, that's more like it.

00:04:28.930 --> 00:04:32.040
But the enemy is moving
faster than I expected...

00:04:32.040 --> 00:04:33.240
What the...

00:04:33.240 --> 00:04:35.740
Now they're gathering here, at the bridge!

00:04:35.740 --> 00:04:38.110
Gambee squads won't make it in time!

00:04:38.110 --> 00:04:42.280
Raise an omni-directional light beacon!
Contact the Strain squadron!

00:04:42.280 --> 00:04:46.270
Destroy the TUMORs gathering
on the bridge! Top priority!

00:04:47.390 --> 00:04:51.080
Damn you, you TUMORs!
You're trying to get inside the bridge?!

00:04:54.990 --> 00:04:55.980
What?!

00:05:03.840 --> 00:05:05.740
Lottie! Are you all right?!

00:05:05.740 --> 00:05:08.740
Somehow or other! You take the bridge!

00:05:08.740 --> 00:05:09.900
Roger!

00:05:18.580 --> 00:05:21.050
I can't get near the bridge like this...

00:05:25.520 --> 00:05:28.860
No! All hands, fall back! Get out of here!

00:05:28.860 --> 00:05:29.730
Quickly!

00:05:29.730 --> 00:05:32.000
Transferring command to the sub-bridge!

00:05:32.000 --> 00:05:33.160
Quickly!

00:05:40.040 --> 00:05:41.640
Jake-kun! Hurry!

00:05:41.640 --> 00:05:44.800
Yes, sir! This should ensure the students-

00:05:52.420 --> 00:05:54.480
Jake!

00:06:01.130 --> 00:06:02.960
The bridge!

00:06:02.960 --> 00:06:05.620
We're not enough to protect it?

00:06:08.800 --> 00:06:12.800
I can't increase its output!
I won't be able to catch him now!

00:06:12.800 --> 00:06:15.570
Lottie! The ship's in trouble! Let's go back!

00:06:15.570 --> 00:06:21.180
Screw that, Dickon! I haven't
taken him - Ralph Werec - down!

00:06:21.180 --> 00:06:24.920
Don't be crazy! You wouldn't
stand a chance in your condition!

00:06:24.920 --> 00:06:28.590
Not to mention only half
of the Strains are left now!

00:06:28.590 --> 00:06:31.090
The Libertad'll be destroyed
if we don't do something!

00:06:31.090 --> 00:06:35.290
And then it'll be all over!
Everyone still alive needs to protect it!

00:06:48.470 --> 00:06:52.430
Brother! Tell me!
Why are you doing this?!

00:07:10.300 --> 00:07:11.460
No, you don't!

00:07:21.540 --> 00:07:23.300
That wasn't a deep cut, but...

00:07:28.110 --> 00:07:29.440
Wait, Brother!

00:07:32.820 --> 00:07:36.650
My Mercurion! I'm out of energy
at a time like this?!

00:07:38.090 --> 00:07:41.690
Stop! You won't make it back
to the ship if you follow him!

00:07:41.690 --> 00:07:43.900
The enemy TUMORs seem
to be retreating, too.

00:07:43.900 --> 00:07:46.530
Being reckless now will only
result in a pointless death!

00:07:46.530 --> 00:07:49.970
I don't care about any of that!
I have to go!

00:07:49.970 --> 00:07:52.070
So let go! Let go of me!

00:07:52.070 --> 00:07:55.200
Please, let go! Let go!

00:08:08.690 --> 00:08:12.990
She's a cadet in the Mobile
Troops Division, not a Reasoner.

00:08:12.990 --> 00:08:15.760
There is no record of her being
a Reasoner in the past, either.

00:08:15.760 --> 00:08:20.900
But she did link with the Mimic
I prepared for the start-up test.

00:08:20.900 --> 00:08:25.200
It's not possible!
Linking with another person's Mimic...

00:08:25.200 --> 00:08:27.770
Yeah... I know.

00:08:27.770 --> 00:08:29.540
That's why I need to conduct research.

00:08:29.540 --> 00:08:30.780
Eh?

00:08:30.780 --> 00:08:34.480
I'd like to look after her until
we know more about who she is.

00:08:34.480 --> 00:08:36.410
No, that's not-

00:08:36.410 --> 00:08:38.680
This is a waste of time. I'm leaving.

00:08:38.680 --> 00:08:40.420
Hold on, now!

00:08:40.420 --> 00:08:43.420
You still need to explain the matter
of creating your own Strain!

00:08:43.420 --> 00:08:45.960
You're as picky about details as always.

00:08:45.960 --> 00:08:49.290
I'm sure you'll figure out the best
course of action. I leave it to you!

00:08:50.430 --> 00:08:53.970
I might say he's more
the same "as always..."

00:08:53.970 --> 00:08:58.740
Well, it's basically thanks to his
unit that we escaped with our lives.

00:08:58.740 --> 00:09:00.670
Perhaps we should overlook this...

00:09:17.260 --> 00:09:18.240
Okay!

00:09:20.990 --> 00:09:24.230
Are you really sure it was
that Gambee girl, Queen?

00:09:24.230 --> 00:09:26.630
Don't come if you don't believe me!

00:09:26.630 --> 00:09:30.500
It was her, Dickon!
I recognized her voice, too.

00:09:30.500 --> 00:09:32.770
Hey, Ermy. What's going on?

00:09:32.770 --> 00:09:36.270
I'm not really sure myself...

00:09:36.270 --> 00:09:37.880
Her!

00:09:37.880 --> 00:09:40.550
There's no major damage,
from what I can see...

00:09:40.550 --> 00:09:43.310
I guess its fuel consumption
is its biggest problem...

00:09:43.310 --> 00:09:46.980
Then I'll just download
the combat data and...

00:09:50.220 --> 00:09:51.220
Can I help you?

00:09:51.220 --> 00:09:53.620
Sara Cruz! I know she's here!

00:10:00.800 --> 00:10:02.670
Was it really you?!

00:10:02.670 --> 00:10:06.270
I'm asking if you were
the one who piloted this Strain!

00:10:06.270 --> 00:10:07.830
Well?!

00:10:12.140 --> 00:10:13.140
W-whoa...

00:10:13.140 --> 00:10:16.780
Why? Why did you hide
the fact you're a Reasoner?

00:10:16.780 --> 00:10:20.770
Why did you transfer here,
pretending to be a Gambee pilot?!

00:10:23.960 --> 00:10:29.060
I'm asking why you lied! Answer me!

00:10:29.060 --> 00:10:32.560
Listen! Just how many people do
you think died in that battle?!

00:10:32.560 --> 00:10:34.370
If this Strain had been
used from the start,

00:10:34.370 --> 00:10:36.500
there would've been fewer casualties!

00:10:36.500 --> 00:10:38.100
So why?!

00:10:38.100 --> 00:10:39.100
I'm not...

00:10:39.100 --> 00:10:41.440
Sara!

00:10:41.440 --> 00:10:43.370
Allow me to answer her question!

00:10:43.370 --> 00:10:44.880
This Strain and Reasoner are top-secret;

00:10:44.880 --> 00:10:47.510
only a few high-ranking
officials know about them.

00:10:47.510 --> 00:10:49.680
What?! I never heard that!

00:10:49.680 --> 00:10:51.480
Well, it is a secret.

00:10:51.480 --> 00:10:54.550
Meaning Sara couldn't say anything,
even if she wanted to.

00:10:54.550 --> 00:10:59.190
Besides, this Strain still wasn't
in combat-ready condition.

00:10:59.190 --> 00:11:03.230
She took it out without
permission to help you all.

00:11:03.230 --> 00:11:05.200
To help us?

00:11:05.200 --> 00:11:06.200
And she's waiting here

00:11:06.200 --> 00:11:09.970
because she's about to get
a lecture about being reckless.

00:11:09.970 --> 00:11:11.300
I see.

00:11:11.300 --> 00:11:16.240
If you hadn't held him back,
we'd probably have been wiped out.

00:11:16.240 --> 00:11:17.730
Thank you.

00:11:20.510 --> 00:11:21.650
Aww, geez!

00:11:21.650 --> 00:11:24.520
Watch yourself now!
This is his usual old method!

00:11:24.520 --> 00:11:25.650
Be quiet, Dickon!

00:11:25.650 --> 00:11:27.490
You're so cute!

00:11:27.490 --> 00:11:29.490
Where have you been hiding all this time?

00:11:29.490 --> 00:11:34.230
It's fate that we've met here!
Please be my friend, okay?!

00:11:34.230 --> 00:11:38.130
--Quit that, Lavinia! You just met her!
--You're such a meanie, Martha!

00:11:38.130 --> 00:11:39.230
Say!

00:11:39.230 --> 00:11:44.000
If you're a secret weapon, does that
mean you're why they attacked?

00:11:44.000 --> 00:11:46.740
Don't be dumb!
I told you, it's a secret!

00:11:46.740 --> 00:11:51.980
I'd never do anything stupid
to let the Deague learn our secrets!

00:11:51.980 --> 00:11:54.680
W-what's with that look?!

00:11:54.680 --> 00:11:57.720
I mean... seriously.

00:11:57.720 --> 00:12:00.250
--Get out, all of you!
--Eh?!

00:12:00.250 --> 00:12:02.350
Instructor's orders!

00:12:02.350 --> 00:12:06.520
--Whoa! What is this thing?!
--Hey, quit it!

00:12:11.460 --> 00:12:13.690
Now, then...

00:12:16.670 --> 00:12:22.440
You losing your Mimic in an accident
doesn't answer anything.

00:12:22.440 --> 00:12:25.510
Have you ever linked with
another person's Mimic before?

00:12:25.510 --> 00:12:26.680
No...

00:12:26.680 --> 00:12:28.710
It is unheard of...

00:12:28.710 --> 00:12:31.220
Why was I able to link with her?

00:12:31.220 --> 00:12:32.580
Good question.

00:12:32.580 --> 00:12:36.790
You're going to transfer into
the Spatial Armor Division now.

00:12:36.790 --> 00:12:39.290
And you're also being put
under our supervision.

00:12:39.290 --> 00:12:40.790
Okay.

00:12:40.790 --> 00:12:44.800
Which means you're going to live here.
Your room will be...

00:12:44.800 --> 00:12:47.330
Well, we'll figure something out.

00:12:47.330 --> 00:12:52.170
Also, don't tell anyone you
linked with someone else's Mimic.

00:12:52.170 --> 00:12:53.040
Okay.

00:12:53.040 --> 00:12:56.940
Listen. That Mimic
and that Strain belong to me.

00:12:56.940 --> 00:13:01.350
Which means you, their Reasoner,
belong to me, too.

00:13:01.350 --> 00:13:02.980
Don't do anything out of line, now.

00:13:02.980 --> 00:13:06.380
Ooh! Sounds naughty!

00:13:06.380 --> 00:13:07.750
Shut up, Carmichael!

00:13:07.750 --> 00:13:09.990
--Naughty, naughty!
--How is that "naughty"?!

00:13:09.990 --> 00:13:11.510
Pervy!

00:13:17.960 --> 00:13:21.030
Ralph Werec's Gloire has returned to ship.

00:13:21.030 --> 00:13:23.870
It seems seizure of the target didn't occur.

00:13:23.870 --> 00:13:27.240
What shall we do now, Captain Medlock?

00:13:27.240 --> 00:13:31.180
Maintain current distance with
the enemy and continue to follow!

00:13:31.180 --> 00:13:32.110
Understood.

00:13:32.110 --> 00:13:34.880
Captain. With all due respect,
if we continue as we are,

00:13:34.880 --> 00:13:38.450
we may be late for the rendezvous
for the next operation.

00:13:38.450 --> 00:13:41.190
Besides, isn't one sample more than enough?

00:13:41.190 --> 00:13:42.890
Never mind that.

00:13:42.890 --> 00:13:46.020
More importantly, hurry and increase
the Mercurion purity level.

00:13:46.020 --> 00:13:49.590
He complains that the Strain
is in bad shape due to poor refinement.

00:13:49.590 --> 00:13:54.370
We use Mercurion in a fundamentally
different way than the Union!

00:13:54.370 --> 00:13:56.070
Our equipment is different!

00:13:56.070 --> 00:14:01.770
Mercurion is nothing but fuel -
using it to control a unit is absurd!

00:14:01.770 --> 00:14:04.740
You've said that countless
times now, Lt. Colonel Barrow.

00:14:04.740 --> 00:14:08.710
You said yourself you don't want
anything undermining the operation.

00:14:08.710 --> 00:14:10.550
I'm returning to my quarters.

00:14:10.550 --> 00:14:13.880
Send Ralph to me. I want
to hear his report in person.

00:14:47.020 --> 00:14:51.020
I see. So you didn't find what
you were looking for, then?

00:14:51.020 --> 00:14:52.160
No.

00:14:52.160 --> 00:14:56.430
Meaning we'll have to strike again.
That'll be troublesome.

00:14:56.430 --> 00:14:57.430
Yes.

00:14:57.430 --> 00:14:59.830
You're certain there's one more?

00:14:59.830 --> 00:15:01.270
Yes.

00:15:01.270 --> 00:15:03.970
I believe you, because you're
the one saying it,

00:15:03.970 --> 00:15:08.270
but I'm taking quite
a risk myself with this.

00:15:08.270 --> 00:15:10.740
So we can't fail.

00:15:10.740 --> 00:15:13.110
Next time for sure, okay?

00:15:17.380 --> 00:15:21.790
It was an unforeseen battle,
but you all did very well.

00:15:21.790 --> 00:15:24.790
Both escort ships accompanying
us were shot down,

00:15:24.790 --> 00:15:28.760
and we lost over half of our
instructors and cadets on this ship.

00:15:28.760 --> 00:15:30.560
Our main bridge was also destroyed,

00:15:30.560 --> 00:15:33.230
but as control has been
transferred to the sub-bridge,

00:15:33.230 --> 00:15:35.730
our navigation has not been affected.

00:15:35.730 --> 00:15:37.470
However, it remains unknown

00:15:37.470 --> 00:15:41.110
why the Deague would attack
an exercise ship such as ours.

00:15:41.110 --> 00:15:46.580
As further enemy attacks are anticipated,
we will now reduce speed

00:15:46.580 --> 00:15:51.080
and make a detour to the Gall
Space Supply Depot, an ally base.

00:15:51.080 --> 00:15:53.220
There, we will repair
and re-supply the ship,

00:15:53.220 --> 00:15:55.790
as well as hand over the injured.

00:15:55.790 --> 00:15:58.220
Until then, I ask that each
and every one of you

00:15:58.220 --> 00:16:02.230
remain constantly alert and ready
to respond to any situation.

00:16:02.230 --> 00:16:03.390
That is all.

00:16:05.300 --> 00:16:08.800
It's just a good thing Gall was nearby...

00:16:08.800 --> 00:16:09.800
Yes.

00:16:09.800 --> 00:16:13.740
But it's originally only
a civilian supply station.

00:16:13.740 --> 00:16:17.780
Might it not be best to seek
protection at the military post

00:16:17.780 --> 00:16:21.250
on Planet Bregma, the first
of our original destinations?

00:16:21.250 --> 00:16:25.780
Indeed. I'd like to be ready
to fight back next time.

00:16:25.780 --> 00:16:29.620
Yes. We will return their favor.

00:16:33.020 --> 00:16:35.260
Moving out already?

00:16:35.260 --> 00:16:37.500
Go on, get the hell out!

00:16:37.500 --> 00:16:40.360
I'll be glad to have this
room all for myself, too!

00:16:51.210 --> 00:16:54.370
You're actually a Reasoner, I hear?

00:16:55.950 --> 00:16:57.110
Yes...

00:17:26.040 --> 00:17:27.910
Brother...

00:17:30.280 --> 00:17:32.280
Who's there?!

00:17:32.280 --> 00:17:33.880
Oh, it's you.

00:17:33.880 --> 00:17:37.260
You caught me at an awkward moment...

00:17:37.260 --> 00:17:39.990
Did you hear that just now?

00:17:39.990 --> 00:17:41.660
I'm sorry...

00:17:41.660 --> 00:17:45.360
No, I don't mind. It's not
something I'm trying to hide.

00:17:46.960 --> 00:17:50.640
I had an older brother who was a Reasoner.

00:17:50.640 --> 00:17:58.380
My dream was to be as great a Reasoner
as him and fight together...

00:17:58.380 --> 00:18:03.450
But... he died on Grabera.

00:18:03.450 --> 00:18:07.350
He was killed by Ralph Werec,
the traitor!

00:18:07.350 --> 00:18:10.080
That's why I have to...

00:18:13.960 --> 00:18:19.860
S-sorry. I always get like this
when I think about my brother...

00:18:19.860 --> 00:18:22.360
Don't tell anyone I cried.

00:18:24.740 --> 00:18:27.400
More harassment?

00:18:31.240 --> 00:18:34.580
I guess you're still as gutsy
a girl as ever...

00:18:43.020 --> 00:18:45.420
Sara! You're finally back!

00:18:45.420 --> 00:18:48.030
I set up a room for you!

00:18:48.030 --> 00:18:51.650
I cleared out that storeroom there.
Use it however you like.

00:19:00.440 --> 00:19:01.770
Emily...

00:19:01.770 --> 00:19:04.940
You two'd prefer being together, right?

00:19:04.940 --> 00:19:09.910
Oh, and I made a dress like the one
in that drawing you did earlier.

00:19:09.910 --> 00:19:11.580
Is that how you want it?

00:19:13.250 --> 00:19:15.240
Yeah. Thanks.

00:19:16.390 --> 00:19:20.020
You're gonna help out with all
sorts of tests starting tomorrow.

00:19:28.370 --> 00:19:30.230
Emily...

00:19:30.230 --> 00:19:33.600
Who are you really?

00:19:33.600 --> 00:19:37.840
Why did you link with me?

00:19:37.840 --> 00:19:42.210
Why did you fight alongside me?

00:19:42.210 --> 00:19:47.550
That person we fought today...
He's my brother.

00:19:47.550 --> 00:19:53.790
My one and only dear brother
in the world. I love him.

00:19:53.790 --> 00:19:57.360
But he changed...

00:19:57.360 --> 00:20:00.400
It's too hard for me to believe.

00:20:00.400 --> 00:20:05.170
My brother is trying to do something,
and has dragged many into it.

00:20:05.170 --> 00:20:08.310
I don't know what he's trying,

00:20:08.310 --> 00:20:12.010
but I don't want to let
him hurt anyone else.

00:20:12.010 --> 00:20:14.680
I want him to be
my gentle brother again...

00:20:14.680 --> 00:20:18.580
So, please. Help me...

00:20:18.580 --> 00:20:21.290
I want to stop my brother...

00:20:21.290 --> 00:20:23.590
Even if...

00:20:23.590 --> 00:20:27.580
Even if it means fighting him...

00:20:31.300 --> 00:20:35.570
I'm not my real self now.
Nor am I fit to be called a friend.

00:20:35.570 --> 00:20:38.200
And then anger collides...

00:20:38.200 --> 00:20:41.570
On the next Soukou no Strain:
Endless Love and Hate

00:20:41.570 --> 00:20:43.230
Satisfied?
